# Line endings.
#
# Everything under deploy/ runs on Linux. A shell script that reaches the VPS
# with CRLF endings fails as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`, and a
# systemd unit or Caddy config with them is rejected or silently misparsed.
#
# Without this file that guarantee rests on each clone's core.autocrlf setting
# — which is per-machine, so a fresh checkout or a CI runner configured
# differently could commit CRLF and break a deploy in a way that looks nothing
# like its cause.

# Normalise text on commit; let git pick the working-copy ending.
* text=auto

# These must be LF in the working copy too, on every platform.
*.sh              text eol=lf
*.template        text eol=lf
*.env             text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf
*.mjs             text eol=lf
Caddyfile         text eol=lf
.deploy-env       text eol=lf
deploy/**         text eol=lf

# PowerShell stays CRLF — it is only ever run on Windows.
*.ps1             text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png             binary
*.jpg             binary
*.jpeg            binary
*.gif             binary
*.webp            binary
*.ico             binary
*.woff            binary
*.woff2           binary
*.pdf             binary
